\ A tail-position `if` whose arm raises from the last call of a loop body, pinned eager. A
\ tail-position `if` reports no row of its own whatever its arm does, as it does interpreted.
\
\ Eager inlines `times`, so the rows inside the loop that the interpreted chain carries are absent
\ here. The absent `go`-level `if` row is what this pins.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ 1 [ boom ] times 0 drop ] [ ] if ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
